            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Robyn Morgan, an hourly employee at a Taco\u202fBell franchise owned by Sundance, Inc., signed an agreement to arbitrate any employment dispute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f9681d83b18ec27196b249b714269cded64cf31c4159df0d45a5463ed299cb1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f9681d83b18-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that it may not create a new procedural rule based on the Federal Arbitration Act\u2019s (FAA) policy favoring arbitration."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f9681d83b18ec27196b249b714269cded64cf31c4159df0d45a5463ed299cb1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f9681d83b18-0000-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, judge Colloton dissented, arguing that Sundance had led Morgan to waste time and money and engaged in fruitless mediation."
      }
