              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner), according to Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner), section\u202f2 of the Federal Arbitration Act requires that an arbitration agreement be enforced unless a generally applicable contract defense makes it unenforceable."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner), according to Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner), sundance intentionally relinquished its contractual arbitration rights by asking a federal judge to dismiss the case and filing an answer that omitted any reference to arbitration; those actions should constitute a waiver and place Sundance in default under Section\u202f3 of the FAA."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MS. GILBRIDE",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0014"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 84,
                "start": 84
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MS. GILBRIDE, there should be no prejudice requirement; the FAA\u2019s structure indicates that waiver questions should be decided in a summary manner."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Robyn Morgan)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Clement, neither the FAA nor Iowa state law supports the petitioner\u2019s rule that a motion to stay litigation in favor of arbitration must be filed expeditiously or be lost forever; Section\u202f3 of the FAA directs courts to grant such motions unless the stay applicant is in default."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 68,
                "start": 68
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. CLEMENT, most circuits follow a two\u2011step analysis: first determine whether the party knew about the arbitration agreement, then assess whether the party acted inconsistently with that agreement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 78,
                "start": 78
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. CLEMENT, incentives should consider the party that first defaults or first violates the arbitration agreement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Sundance",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0004-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 85,
                "start": 85
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Sundance argues that the appropriate standard for staying litigation should be \u201csubstantial participation in discovery.\u201d"
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent (Sundance, Inc.)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
